  "query_preview": "..FOR EXTREME SOUTHWESTERN CALIFORNIA INCLUDING ORANGE...\nSAN DIEGO...WESTERN RIVERSIDE AND SOUTHWESTERN SAN BERNARDINO\nCOUNTIES...\n\n...UPDATED AVIATION DISCUSSION...\n\nTonight through Thursday...\n\nA ridge is building back in over the region as the upper level low \nthat was positioned over Arizona continues to propagate eastward. \nThis is going to allow for the positively-tilted ridge to continue \nto expand back towards the northeast. This will result in \ntemperatures gradually increasing through Thursday. Gusty northerly \nwinds will continue to diminish as the low pulls away, but remain \ngusty each afternoon through tomorrow, especially within the San \nGorgonio Pass. For tonight, there will be a little better onshore \nflow this evening, which will allow for the marine layer to likely \nset in a little sooner and also fill in better into the inland \nareas. Ceilings will begin to lower a bit throughout the night, and \nthere may also be some areas of patchy fog along the I-15 corridor \nagain, as there was this morning. For tomorrow, highs will be around \n10 to 15 degrees above the seasonal average, and relative humidities \nwill still be relatively higher at night, and therefore nights will \nstill be close to average.\n\nFriday through Wednesday...\n\nBy Friday, the ridge is going to continue to strengthen to heights \nof 590 dm over the region, which is going to cause temperatures to \nmax out generally around 15 to 20 degrees above the seasonal \naverage. This, in combination with increasing RH values, which will \nnot allow for radiational cooling to cool temperatures as much, will \nproduce conditions that may be impactful for those sensitive to \nthose vulnerable to heat, especially for those along the coastal \nareas that do not have AC units. For this reason, an Extreme Heat \nWatch has been issued for the coastal and inland valleys from Friday \nthrough the mid part of next week. Temperatures are going to become \neven hotter for this upcoming weekend, and on Sunday there will \nbe easterly winds as the position of the high slides further south\nover the desert southwest by Sunday. These offshore winds will \nlikely result in highs being even further warmer to the coast. \nThese gusty easterly downsloping winds will also reduce RH values \ndown into the 15-25% range for the inland areas and elevate fire \nconcerns. As the ridge remains locked in place going into the mid \npart of next week, so will the heat, and there will not be much \nrelief from this looking into the foreseeable future until the \nridge begins to finally break down.",
